WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.711
Welcome to Module 2 Designing Relational Databases
In this module we

00:00:05.737 --> 00:00:09.079
are going to focus on the structure that makes
reliable SQL and

00:00:09.105 --> 00:00:14.807
analytics possible later Before we worry about
writing long queries we

00:00:14.833 --> 00:00:18.426
need to decide what each table represents what one
row means how

00:00:18.452 --> 00:00:24.216
tables connect and what rules the database should
protect automatically The

00:00:24.242 --> 00:00:28.242
examples use a small outpatient clinic but the
design ideas apply to

00:00:28.255 --> 00:00:34.383
many domains such as retail education finance and
operations You

00:00:34.409 --> 00:00:38.764
will also see small PostgreSQL examples that run
directly in the browser

00:00:39.688 --> 00:00:43.109
When a code slide appears run it here first inspect
the result

00:00:43.333 --> 00:00:46.280
and if you want more practice use Copy and paste the
same

00:00:46.307 --> 00:00:51.924
SQL into the pgAdmin Query Tool The goal is not to
memorize

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:56.796
a complete schema The goal is to understand the
design decisions behind

00:00:56.809 --> 00:00:57.427
the schema
